<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pindale Min</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1648–1661</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pindale Min was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/restored-toungoo-kingdom">Restored Toungoo dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1648 to 1661, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thalun">Thalun</a>. His reign was troubled by the arrival of the fugitive Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongli-emperor">Yongli Emperor</a> and by Ming loyalist armies that raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a>. Blamed for the court's failure to defend the country, he was overthrown and killed in 1661 by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pye-min">Pye Min</a>.</p></div>
